--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data under separate terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bundled datasets are NOT covered by the licence above. A component that ships data
under different terms states them separately in its own package metadata — see
AGENTS.md section 8c. Most notably, the NMR predictor plugin's shift database is
derived from nmrshiftdb2 and carries that database's own attribution and share-alike
obligations; describing such a package by its code licence alone is incorrect.

The pKa model's weights are trained in this repository and carry this repo's licence,
but the DATA they were trained on does not. The shipped corpus is 12,096 labelled sites
drawn from FOUR sources; a fifth is recorded and deliberately unused. None is vendored:

  Dwar-iBond experimental pKa set, as distributed with Uni-pKa
  https://github.com/dptech-corp/Uni-pKa -- Apache-2.0
  Values are measurements attributed per row in the source, predominantly
  DataWarrior with literature DOIs for the remainder. RECORDED AS UNRESOLVED: the
  DataWarrior author has stated that the original literature references for part of
  this set were lost, and a software licence is not automatically a licence for an
  associated dataset. This must be settled before public redistribution.

  QupKake experimental pKa set
  https://github.com/Shualdon/QupKake -- CC BY 4.0, ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED
  Originally Baltruschat & Czodrowski. The values are measurements; the per-site
  index is ChemAxon Marvin's assignment and is recorded as such on every row.
  BSD-3-Clause is QupKake's SOFTWARE licence and does not reach this dataset --
  a repository's code licence is not a grant over the data inside it, the same
  distinction recorded for Dwar-iBond above. See docs/benchmarks/pka/pka-provenance.md.

  pKaCHU
  https://zenodo.org/records/20089807 -- CC BY 4.0
  Experimental aqueous values as acid/base microstate pairs. Attribution required.

  D2A-pKa (AQUEOUS ROWS ONLY)
  https://zenodo.org/records/15277342 -- CC BY 4.0
  Attribution required. Only the neat-water rows are used; the DMSO, acetonitrile,
  DMF and alcohol rows are a different measurement scale and are excluded.

  IUPAC Dissociation-Constants v2.3e
  https://zenodo.org/records/21533589 -- CC BY-NC 4.0, NON-COMMERCIAL
  NOT USED BY ANY SHIPPED WEIGHT. The ingest is vendored and the data was evaluated;
  it is the only source carrying weakly basic nitrogens in the numbers this model
  needs, and it degrades the macroscopic fold on amino acids, so it is out. Recorded
  here because that decision could be revisited: were it ever included, the
  NonCommercial term would become a real constraint on redistributing the resulting
  weights under this repository's own licence, and that must be settled before any
  public release rather than discovered afterwards.
